Provenance and modifications
============================

This project is a fork of DeepSeek's open-source chat demo:

  https://github.com/deepseek-ai/chat-demo
  Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek
  Licensed under the MIT License reproduced above.

The fork keeps the original MIT terms and adds the modifications below,
Copyright (c) 2026 the fork authors, released under the same MIT License:

  - a local memory library: always-injected "core" memories plus
    question-scoped retrieval (BM25 over Chinese/English text, optional
    hybrid vector search through an OpenAI-compatible embedding endpoint);
  - model-driven memory tools so the assistant can search, create, revise and
    delete memories, with revision guards, an audit log and undo;
  - per-reply token and prompt-cache usage display;
  - a configurable assistant avatar shown on the welcome screen and on every
    reply;
  - safety_check lowered from "high" to "low";
  - an Android WebView wrapper (android/), brand assets and the
    "Forge Me Not" application name.

See NOTICE for a short summary. The upstream repository, its protocol notes
and the DeepSeek API documentation remain the reference for the API
behaviour that this demo exercises.

